### ⚠️ Statement issue found (highest-value output)
**`ParametricLocal.tendstoInMeasure_supCDFDist_parametric_plugIn` is under-specified — needs `IsCDF (Jlim θ)` (or boundedness of `Jlim θ`).** Its conclusion compares `Jpar n θ̂` with `Jpar n θ`; the only available bridge is `Jlim θ` via the triangle inequality, and any pointwise extraction from `hlocunif` requires `Jlim θ` bounded. The signature supplies only `hlim_cont`. By `Real.iSup_of_not_bddAbove`, an **unbounded** continuous `Jlim θ` makes every `supCDFDist (·) (Jlim θ) = 0` (junk `sSup`), so `hlocunif` holds *vacuously* while the conclusion can fail for arbitrary CDF-valued `Jpar`. This is left as a documented `sorry` with the full note in-file. Note the downstream `…_parametric_bootstrap` *does* carry `hlim_cdf`, so I **proved it directly** (inlined tightness argument) rather than routing through the flawed `plugIn`.

